---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';

/*
 * NOTE: this is a good-faith, factually-accurate template describing what
 * this site actually does. It is not legal advice. If you add analytics,
 * cookies, embedded third-party content, a contact form, or payments,
 * update this page — those all change what you must disclose.
 */

const host = new URL(SITE.domain).host;
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} handles information when you visit ${host}.`}
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="muted small">Last updated: {SITE.privacyUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      This policy explains what information is collected when you visit
      <strong>{host}</strong> (the &ldquo;Site&rdquo;), why it is collected, and what
      you can do about it.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      The Site is operated by {SITE.legalEntity}, based in {SITE.country}
      (&ldquo;I&rdquo;, &ldquo;me&rdquo;). For the purposes of applicable data protection
      law, {SITE.legalEntity} is the controller of any personal data described below.
    </p>
    <p>
      Questions or requests: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What is collected</h2>
    <p>
      The Site is a set of static pages. It does not use cookies, does not run
      analytics, and does not include advertising or third-party tracking scripts.
    </p>

    <h3>2.1 Server logs</h3>
    <p>
      Like virtually all websites, the Site is served through a content delivery
      network, which records basic technical information for each request. This
      typically includes:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>your IP address;</li>
      <li>the date and time of your request;</li>
      <li>the page or file requested;</li>
      <li>your browser type and operating system (user agent);</li>
      <li>the page that referred you, if any.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      These records are generated automatically as a technical necessity of serving
      web pages. They are not used to build a profile of you, and they are not
      combined with information from any other source.
    </p>

    <h3>2.2 What you send me directly</h3>
    <p>
      If you email me, I receive your email address and whatever you choose to
      include in your message. I use it only to reply to you.
    </p>

    <h3>2.3 What is not collected</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>No cookies or local storage are set for tracking purposes.</li>
      <li>No analytics, advertising, or fingerprinting services are used.</li>
      <li>No account registration, and no payment or financial data.</li>
      <li>No location data, and no access to your device beyond the request above.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Why it is processed</h2>
    <p>
      Server logs are processed on the basis of legitimate interests: operating the
      Site securely, keeping it available, and defending against abuse such as
      denial-of-service attacks. Information you email to me is processed in order
      to respond to you, and on the basis of your consent in contacting me.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Who it is shared with</h2>
    <p>
      I do not sell, rent, or trade personal data. Information is shared only with
      the infrastructure provider that hosts and delivers the Site:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong> &mdash; provides hosting, DNS, TLS
        certificates, and content delivery for the Site, and therefore processes
        request data on my behalf as a processor. Cloudflare&rsquo;s own handling of
        this data is described in its
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Data may also be disclosed where I am legally required to do so.
    </p>

    <h2>5. How long it is kept</h2>
    <p>
      Server logs at the delivery network are retained for a short period for
      security and operational purposes and are then discarded. Emails you send me
      are kept for as long as needed to handle your enquiry, and are deleted when no
      longer required. Nothing here is retained indefinitely for marketing purposes,
      because there is no marketing.
    </p>

    <h2>6. International transfers</h2>
    <p>
      The Site is delivered through a global network, so a request from your device
      may be handled by a data centre located outside {SITE.country}. Cloudflare
      maintains contractual safeguards for such transfers as described in its own
      privacy documentation.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have the right to: access the personal
      data held about you; have it corrected; have it erased; object to or restrict
      its processing; receive it in a portable format; and lodge a complaint with
      your local data protection authority.
    </p>
    <p>
      Because this Site collects almost nothing, in most cases there will be no
      stored personal data to act on &mdash; but you are welcome to ask. Write to
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and I will respond within a
      reasonable period.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Children</h2>
    <p>
      The Site is not directed at children and does not knowingly collect personal
      data from them.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Security</h2>
    <p>
      The Site is served exclusively over HTTPS. Traffic is encrypted in transit.
      No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, but the amount of
      personal data involved here is deliberately minimal.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the &ldquo;last updated&rdquo; date at the top of this
      page will change with it. Continued use of the Site after an update means you
      accept the revised policy.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.legalEntity}<br />
      {SITE.country}<br />
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
